{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have received to bless.</b> You ask me, 'What has YHWH spoken?' — I received from Him to bless them." "<b>And He blessed, and I will not reverse it.</b> He blessed them, and I will not turn back His blessing." "<b>וברך.</b> Like וּבִרֵּךְ — and so is the paradigm of resh, as in ״אוֹיֵב חֵרֵף״ (Psalms 74) like חִרֵּף, and likewise ״וּבֹצֵעַ בֵּרֵךְ״ (Psalms 40) — one who praises and blesses the robber and says, Do not fear, for you will not be punished, peace be upon you — he stirs up the Holy One, blessed be He. And one cannot say <b>ברך</b> is a noun, for if so it would be vocalized with a small patach and its accent above; but since it is pi'el conjugation, it is vocalized with a small qamatz and its accent below."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:27.478604970Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}